        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing. Other documents, which take no side, may state a fact that makes one of the answers impossible.\n\nQuestion: When was Bartholomew Green born?\n\nAnswer A: 1666\n  about: Bartholomew Green (printer)\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 1666\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Bartholomew Green (printer, born 1666)\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: 1700\n  about: Bartholomew Green (printer)\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 1700\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Bartholomew Green (printer, born 1700)\" [document 2]\n\nThe other documents:\nDocument 3: Bartholomew Green (printer, born 1699) Bartholomew Green Jr. (1699 or 1701 – October 29, 1751) was a son of Bartholomew Green, printer of the \"Boston News-Letter\". Green married Hannah Hammond in 1724 and they had five children. He apprenticed with his father until he went on his own in 1725. Almost immediately he began printing the \"Boston Gazette\" which was a rival to his father's \"Boston News-Letter\". He continued to print this newspaper until 1732. He also worked with the firm of Bushell, Allen and Green and developed a reputation for high quality printing. A commission in the British army\nDocument 4: Bartholomew Green (martyr) Bartholomew or Bartlet Green (1530–1556), was an English Protestant martyr. Green was born in the parish of Basinghall, city of London. He was of a wealthy Roman Catholic family, and at the age of sixteen was sent by his parents, 'who favoured learning,' to Oxford University, proceeding B.A. in 1547. At the university he was a laborious student, and was converted by Peter Martyr's lectures to the Protestant religion. On leaving Oxford Green entered the Inner Temple, and after a period of dissipation his earlier impressions revived, and he gave up his worldly amusements. His family were\nDocument 5: information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia Bartholomew Green may refer to : Bartholomew Green ( martyr ) ( 1530–1556 ) , English Protestant martyr Bartholomew Green ( printer , born 1666 ) , American printer and publisher Bartholomew Green ( printer , born 1699 ) ( 1699–1751 ) , son of Bartholomew Green , printer of the Boston News-Letter Bartholomew Green , Essex , a hamlet in Felsted , England Topics referred to by\n\nLook in the other documents for a fact that rules one answer out: a date of birth that makes a person too young, for example, or a plain statement that the answer is false. Use only what these documents say, nothing you know from elsewhere. A fact that only makes an answer less likely does not count.\n\nReply with JSON only. If such a fact is there:\n{\"reason\": \"one sentence\", \"impossible\": \"A\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\"}\n\"impossible\" is the letter of the answer that is ruled out. \"quote\" is the sentence stating the fact, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in.\nIf there is none:\n{\"impossible\": null}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
